WEBVTT

00:08.230 --> 00:16.450
Natsume Yujin-cho Go

01:34.680 --> 01:36.560
I was on my way back from an errand

01:36.560 --> 01:39.110
that Touko-san had asked me
to do in the next town.

01:39.110 --> 01:42.420
I'd tried to take a shortcut and gotten lost.

02:07.990 --> 02:08.980
Hatsuna!

02:22.950 --> 02:24.880
It's Natsume Reiko!

02:24.880 --> 02:26.020
Reiko?

02:40.510 --> 02:44.510
One

02:40.510 --> 02:44.510
Night's

02:40.510 --> 02:44.510
Cups

02:50.170 --> 02:52.300
Reiko! Are you okay?

02:52.810 --> 02:55.790
Oh, you're awake, Reiko!

02:55.790 --> 02:57.780
No, I'm...

02:58.170 --> 03:04.490
I'm sorry. That One-Horn got angry just
because he got close to Bousui Rock...

03:04.490 --> 03:07.620
That's why I said we didn't need that thing!

03:07.620 --> 03:09.660
But aren't you curious? I am!

03:09.660 --> 03:11.420
It's almost time!

03:12.670 --> 03:15.650
Oh, they say that it's almost
time for the water from

03:15.650 --> 03:18.370
Bousui Rock to make the one
who drinks it more powerful,

03:18.370 --> 03:21.300
an event which happens
once every twelve years.

03:21.300 --> 03:25.470
That big thing wants it all for himself.

03:25.470 --> 03:27.060
What a jerk.

03:27.060 --> 03:29.410
Does your head still hurt?

03:29.410 --> 03:32.020
No, I'm okay now.

03:39.890 --> 03:41.840
You saved me and brought me here?

03:41.840 --> 03:44.840
You're the one who saved us.

03:44.840 --> 03:47.100
You're as amazing as they say, Natsume Reiko!

03:47.100 --> 03:50.450
You drove that thing off with a single punch!

03:50.450 --> 03:53.580
Wait, I'm not Reiko-san.

03:55.310 --> 03:57.400
I'm Natsume Takashi, her grandson.

03:57.400 --> 03:59.730
Reiko-san passed away years ago.

03:59.730 --> 04:00.630
Grandson?

04:00.630 --> 04:01.830
Passed away?

04:01.830 --> 04:03.970
She's gone.

04:03.970 --> 04:06.060
Maybe she hit her head...

04:06.060 --> 04:08.200
Rest a bit more, Reiko.

04:08.200 --> 04:09.820
It's true.

04:09.820 --> 04:11.950
I've never even met my grandmother.

04:14.100 --> 04:18.080
Hey, can you tell me about Reiko-san?

04:18.800 --> 04:23.000
I told you something seemed off!

04:23.000 --> 04:24.020
What?

04:24.020 --> 04:26.660
You said this smell was definitely Reiko!
You were sure of it!

04:26.660 --> 04:30.320
You had a huge fit and said Reiko might die!

04:31.690 --> 04:34.080
Oh, I see...

04:34.080 --> 04:35.780
So Reiko's gone...

04:37.020 --> 04:39.450
That's a shame...

04:39.450 --> 04:42.460
We should've come sooner...

04:44.400 --> 04:47.290
The two of us, husband
and wife, are travelers.

04:47.820 --> 04:48.970
Husband and wife.

04:49.330 --> 04:54.370
We met Reiko here, so we thought
we could meet her again.

04:56.690 --> 05:00.200
The two of us make sake cups.

05:00.200 --> 05:03.490
We make them in a kiln wherever we go.

05:03.490 --> 05:06.240
Hey, what's that?

05:06.800 --> 05:09.750
A child of man, talking to us!

05:09.750 --> 05:13.230
Are you Natsume Reiko, the
girl everyone's talking about?

05:13.230 --> 05:15.650
What? A girl like this?

05:15.650 --> 05:16.900
How rude.

05:16.900 --> 05:18.500
She answered!

05:19.300 --> 05:21.510
This is a kiln, right?

05:22.040 --> 05:23.310
Yeah.

05:23.310 --> 05:26.010
We're about to fire the sake cups.

05:26.440 --> 05:30.080
Reiko, if you're free, want to fight me?

05:30.080 --> 05:32.960
If I win, you have to drink with me.

05:32.960 --> 05:36.020
If I win, you can have my name or a sake cup.

05:36.020 --> 05:37.010
So you can drink—

05:37.010 --> 05:39.650
Hey, stop being so stupid, honey!

05:39.650 --> 05:41.020
This is my fight!

05:41.020 --> 05:42.260
You stay out of it!

05:42.260 --> 05:44.220
There's no way you could win!

05:44.220 --> 05:47.530
You two are really close, huh?

05:48.150 --> 05:50.010
See? She's laughing at you!

05:52.470 --> 05:57.410
Sorry, but humans can't
drink until they're grow-ups,

05:57.410 --> 05:59.850
so no fighting.

06:01.080 --> 06:05.670
I was looking forward to drinking with
Reiko when she became this "grown-up."

06:07.130 --> 06:09.250
Well, but you know...

06:09.250 --> 06:12.730
It must be Reiko that forged the
fate that brought us together,

06:12.730 --> 06:15.220
and caused you to save us.

06:15.220 --> 06:18.110
Natsume, rest here as long as you like.

06:18.110 --> 06:19.130
That's right.

06:19.130 --> 06:20.820
Don't push yourself.

06:20.820 --> 06:24.190
I know! Natsume, you want some water?

06:24.190 --> 06:26.300
Yeah, thanks.

06:26.920 --> 06:31.570
Aww, so you're still a kid
who can't drink, either?

06:33.500 --> 06:34.800
Here you go.

06:36.950 --> 06:40.210
Did you two make this cup?

06:47.340 --> 06:48.970
It's good!

06:50.260 --> 06:52.990
It's the power of the One Night Cup!

06:52.990 --> 06:54.970
It makes sake taste even better!

06:54.970 --> 06:57.290
If you drink sake with the cups we make,

06:57.290 --> 07:00.020
it will taste delicious,
no matter what kind of sake it is!

07:01.510 --> 07:03.480
I bet Sensei would love this...

07:03.480 --> 07:05.340
Everybody says it doesn't just taste good,

07:05.340 --> 07:07.550
it makes them feel powerful!

07:07.550 --> 07:08.240
Yeah.

07:08.240 --> 07:11.900
Yeah, I feel stronger somehow.

07:11.900 --> 07:13.910
Right? Right?

07:13.910 --> 07:17.240
He forms them, and I glaze them,

07:17.240 --> 07:20.590
and it gives them this strange power.

07:20.590 --> 07:22.750
But it disappears in a night.

07:24.130 --> 07:26.030
It disappears?

07:26.570 --> 07:28.430
Funny, huh?

07:28.430 --> 07:31.590
So they started calling these One Night Cups,

07:31.590 --> 07:34.100
and everybody loves them.

07:34.100 --> 07:37.000
That's a test fire we just made.

07:37.000 --> 07:39.450
It's well-made.

07:39.450 --> 07:42.020
We'll make a lot more tomorrow.

07:45.010 --> 07:47.360
As we travel,

07:47.360 --> 07:51.650
we make these cups for the youkai we meet.

07:51.650 --> 07:56.550
And we always look forward to the sake
and snacks they give us in exchange...

07:56.550 --> 07:59.160
We have a party almost every night.

07:59.400 --> 08:01.750
And as the night goes on,

08:01.750 --> 08:05.420
we hear more and more stories,
which is the most fun thing of all.

08:05.420 --> 08:07.350
No matter where we go,

08:07.350 --> 08:12.170
youkai hear about the One Night Cups
and come in huge numbers.

08:13.180 --> 08:16.190
Well, some of them are bad news,

08:16.190 --> 08:19.850
and come to interrupt us, or start fights.

08:19.850 --> 08:23.810
And because of that, the two of us have
become quite strong on our journey.

08:25.100 --> 08:27.820
I know. Help me a little, Natsume.

08:29.010 --> 08:32.920
What? Natsume still needs to rest!

08:32.920 --> 08:34.560
I'm fine now.

08:34.560 --> 08:36.540
I want to thank you for
what you've done for me,

08:36.540 --> 08:37.830
but I have to get home.

08:37.830 --> 08:39.450
Can I come back tomorrow?

08:39.450 --> 08:41.570
Yes, that would be great.

08:41.570 --> 08:42.220
Hey.

08:42.220 --> 08:43.120
Right-o!

08:43.720 --> 08:45.460
I'll take you home, Natsume.

08:47.030 --> 08:49.660
Sorry about all that, Natsume.

08:49.660 --> 08:51.680
Hizuchi is so stubborn.

08:51.680 --> 08:53.670
And he's so blunt, too.

08:53.670 --> 08:55.470
You must have felt exasperated, right?

08:55.470 --> 08:56.470
No.

08:56.860 --> 08:58.780
Have you two always been together?

08:58.780 --> 08:59.900
That's right.

08:59.900 --> 09:01.950
For a long long time now.

09:01.950 --> 09:05.760
We've made these cups
together for a long time.

09:05.760 --> 09:09.290
But it's quite rare for him
to ask anybody else for help.

09:09.290 --> 09:14.240
He's never let anybody else touch the clay.

09:14.240 --> 09:15.680
Is that true?

09:15.680 --> 09:16.960
He's being stubborn,

09:16.960 --> 09:19.240
but it's possible he's
feeling a little weak-kneed.

09:20.450 --> 09:24.250
If only time would stop for just a little...

09:24.820 --> 09:28.080
He loves making cups so much.

09:29.080 --> 09:30.140
Oh, sorry.

09:30.140 --> 09:31.640
It's nothing.

09:31.640 --> 09:35.480
Hizuchi must've been really
happy to meet you, Natsume.

09:35.480 --> 09:37.400
I know I am.

09:37.400 --> 09:38.760
Come tomorrow.

09:39.150 --> 09:40.510
Oh, look!

09:41.220 --> 09:42.940
That's one of the human paths ahead.

09:42.940 --> 09:44.020
You're okay now, right?

09:44.020 --> 09:45.410
Got it.

09:45.410 --> 09:46.980
Thanks, Hatsuna.

09:49.270 --> 09:52.520
Bye, take care!

09:56.580 --> 09:57.640
I'm back!

09:57.640 --> 09:58.820
Sorry I'm late!

09:58.820 --> 10:00.280
Welcome back!

10:00.600 --> 10:03.000
Sorry, I got lost.

10:03.000 --> 10:05.520
I see.

10:05.520 --> 10:07.430
Thanks for going all that way.

10:07.430 --> 10:08.130
It was nothing.

10:08.130 --> 10:09.470
Welcome back, Takashi.

10:09.470 --> 10:10.290
Thanks.

10:19.050 --> 10:21.800
What?! The One Night Cups?

10:21.800 --> 10:23.560
I figured you'd know about them.

10:25.040 --> 10:29.340
A sake cup like a dream
that disappears after a single night.

10:29.340 --> 10:32.820
And they say the sake tastes
so good it's like a dream, too.

10:34.840 --> 10:39.500
I've heard that couple has been making
those cups for over a century.

10:39.500 --> 10:40.400
That long?

10:40.400 --> 10:45.510
Every sake drinker in the
world wants to try one!

10:45.510 --> 10:47.090
Let's go now, Natsume!

10:47.090 --> 10:48.390
It's late.

10:48.390 --> 10:49.440
We'll go tomorrow.

10:51.430 --> 10:54.250
No, no, no!

10:53.340 --> 10:54.250
Goodnight.

10:54.250 --> 10:56.280
I want to drink sake!

10:58.090 --> 11:02.600
Why? Why can't I go? Tell me!

10:59.600 --> 11:01.430
I don't know why,

11:01.430 --> 11:03.580
but those two reminded me of old memories.

11:04.800 --> 11:06.850
Hatsuna and Hizuchi,

11:06.850 --> 11:10.690
the two of them always together...

11:14.830 --> 11:17.520
I can't even sleep!

11:17.520 --> 11:18.390
Sake!

11:18.390 --> 11:20.480
Someone bring me sake!

11:25.010 --> 11:28.240
It's the perfect day for a drink!

11:28.240 --> 11:29.410
What are you talking about?

11:29.410 --> 11:33.570
Who would've thought that the
One Night Cups were so close, though?

11:35.260 --> 11:38.150
This is the smell of sake! I know it!

11:36.890 --> 11:39.170
Hey! Sensei!

11:39.170 --> 11:42.680
Sake! Sake! Sake!

11:46.980 --> 11:49.370
Hey, I haven't seen you before.

11:49.370 --> 11:51.060
Did you come for the banquet, too?

11:51.060 --> 11:53.090
Yup. Let me join you.

11:53.090 --> 11:54.390
With pleasure!

11:54.390 --> 11:55.190
Sensei!

11:55.190 --> 11:57.520
Oh, there's a child of man with you?

11:57.520 --> 12:01.200
That was nice of you to bring a snack.

12:01.520 --> 12:04.670
You can't eat him.
He's all tendons and skin!

12:04.670 --> 12:06.830
He'll ruin the good sake!

12:07.250 --> 12:09.500
Yeah, he doesn't look like he'd taste good!

12:11.390 --> 12:13.080
Natsume!

12:15.240 --> 12:16.470
Hatsuna!

12:16.470 --> 12:18.710
Welcome, Natsume!

12:18.710 --> 12:21.340
Hey, give me a sake cup.

12:21.340 --> 12:24.300
Sensei, don't be rude!

12:24.300 --> 12:27.210
Oh, you know Natsume?

12:27.210 --> 12:31.350
The cups are right over here, Mr. Bean Bun.

12:31.350 --> 12:33.050
Who are you calling a bean bun?

12:33.050 --> 12:34.600
Call me Nyanko-sensei!

12:34.600 --> 12:37.610
Now take whichever you like.

12:38.580 --> 12:40.470
Which do I want?

12:40.470 --> 12:42.220
The biggest I can find?

12:42.220 --> 12:46.120
Or is it more important to have something
that fits easily into the hand?

12:47.120 --> 12:48.150
Hizuchi.

12:48.150 --> 12:49.500
Oh, Natsume!

12:49.500 --> 12:51.120
Welcome! Welcome!

12:51.440 --> 12:53.240
The banquet's already started, huh?

12:54.260 --> 12:58.340
The ones who can't wait for
evening gather like that.

12:58.340 --> 13:00.850
I can't wait to drink, too.

13:01.380 --> 13:03.370
But I've still got more cups to make.

13:03.370 --> 13:05.260
Want to try, Natsume?

13:06.090 --> 13:06.990
Sure.

13:07.670 --> 13:08.960
More!

13:08.960 --> 13:10.510
Put more power into it!

13:13.230 --> 13:14.630
I didn't think it would be this heavy!

13:14.630 --> 13:19.170
Hey, don't let me catch you
trying to push Natsume too hard!

13:19.170 --> 13:21.400
What? Get lost!

13:23.740 --> 13:27.160
You're good at that!

13:28.540 --> 13:30.580
Maybe I'll have Natsume take over for me.

13:30.580 --> 13:31.940
What are you talking about?

13:36.170 --> 13:39.300
My wife can be so annoying.

13:39.300 --> 13:41.740
But she's so silly, too, at times.

13:41.740 --> 13:43.360
The clay is nice.

13:43.360 --> 13:44.940
It doesn't talk.

13:45.920 --> 13:48.700
I've been with them a long time.

13:48.700 --> 13:51.560
Both my wife and the clay.

13:52.820 --> 13:56.210
He loves making cups so much.

14:04.920 --> 14:07.700
Now it's my turn.

14:08.200 --> 14:10.650
I glaze them with this.

14:10.650 --> 14:13.420
This part is up to me!

14:13.420 --> 14:14.950
Natsume,

14:14.950 --> 14:17.710
I'm going to fire them!

14:18.780 --> 14:20.960
This is the most important part.

14:20.960 --> 14:24.030
The quality of the fire
controls how they turn out.

14:26.930 --> 14:30.350
You really are like Reiko.

14:31.790 --> 14:36.380
That was the first time
I ever talked to a human.

14:41.020 --> 14:43.050
Hey, Reiko!

14:43.050 --> 14:45.260
Well, are you a grown-up yet?

14:52.670 --> 14:55.620
Hey, are you still not a grown-up?

14:57.230 --> 14:59.980
All she'd ever do was laugh.

15:02.410 --> 15:06.290
They say human lives are short.

15:06.290 --> 15:08.610
It's so frustrating.

15:10.490 --> 15:12.830
It's so strange...

15:16.600 --> 15:23.900
I can't even imagine how
long your journey has been,

15:24.600 --> 15:29.310
but it's amazing that you were able
to get strong during that time.

15:29.860 --> 15:32.530
It's not just getting strong.

15:35.050 --> 15:36.390
It's nothing...

15:40.470 --> 15:42.540
My cup...

15:47.930 --> 15:49.010
What?

15:50.580 --> 15:52.800
So they didn't last until night, huh?

15:55.970 --> 15:59.370
I'm sorry, everyone,
but that's all for today.

15:59.370 --> 16:00.430
I'm sorry.

16:00.430 --> 16:02.790
It's over already?

16:02.790 --> 16:05.690
The night was just getting started, too.

16:05.690 --> 16:08.780
It was good sake, though.

16:08.780 --> 16:09.940
Thank you.

16:11.120 --> 16:12.570
It was great sake.

16:12.570 --> 16:13.820
Thank you.

16:15.560 --> 16:18.700
The sake was even better than I'd heard.

16:19.820 --> 16:20.810
Hey!

16:21.270 --> 16:22.540
Hey!

16:22.540 --> 16:24.830
What? I know!

16:30.330 --> 16:33.130
It's a shame, but it looks
like they don't have

16:33.130 --> 16:35.840
the power to make those cups anymore.

16:36.880 --> 16:39.100
But why?

16:39.800 --> 16:42.100
Nothing happened.

16:42.100 --> 16:45.850
They're just reaching the end of their lives.

16:47.800 --> 16:52.360
Oh, but the end isn't as
soon as you think it is.

16:55.170 --> 16:59.370
If only time would stop for just a little...

16:59.370 --> 17:02.500
It's not just getting strong.

17:02.500 --> 17:09.500
Maybe they were here in search of the
spring water from Bousui Rock.

17:09.500 --> 17:13.800
I think I heard it only
comes once every twelve years,

17:13.800 --> 17:16.740
on the closest night of the full moon.

17:18.200 --> 17:19.770
So that's tonight, huh?

17:25.190 --> 17:28.100
Hey! I was just feeling good!

17:28.100 --> 17:29.270
Don't make me run!

17:39.710 --> 17:42.410
Sensei, take me to Bousui Rock.

18:08.900 --> 18:10.680
Hatsuna! Hizuchi!

18:11.690 --> 18:13.770
You're in the way, child of man.

18:13.770 --> 18:15.190
I'll eat you first!

18:15.490 --> 18:17.450
What are you doing here, Natsume?

18:30.480 --> 18:33.130
He drank his fill of water and got stronger,

18:33.130 --> 18:35.390
but he's no match for me!

18:35.390 --> 18:36.950
He's just another wimp!

18:36.950 --> 18:38.230
Now begone!

18:46.720 --> 18:48.510
I'm sorry, Natsume!

18:48.510 --> 18:50.760
You saved us again...

18:50.760 --> 18:52.980
Thank you, too, Sensei.

18:52.980 --> 18:56.110
Nah, I owed you for the drink.

18:56.110 --> 19:00.990
Natsume, you have a
powerful friend, don't you?

19:14.160 --> 19:19.010
I wanted to mix this water into the glaze.

19:19.010 --> 19:23.260
Thanks to you, we can make our cups again.

19:25.980 --> 19:27.270
I see.

19:27.270 --> 19:30.570
We'd always said that if we
couldn't make them anymore,

19:30.570 --> 19:32.290
we'd just give up.

19:32.290 --> 19:34.230
But she just wouldn't shut up about it...

19:34.230 --> 19:37.280
What? I'm doing this for you...

19:37.280 --> 19:39.190
I know! That's why...

19:39.190 --> 19:43.590
Let's make our sake cups together,
with that, just for the two of us!

19:47.320 --> 19:50.160
I've been thinking...

19:50.940 --> 19:54.260
We've made thousands,
maybe tens of thousands, of these cups.

19:54.260 --> 19:58.620
But we've never made any for ourselves.

19:58.620 --> 20:02.930
For the first and last time,
we can make our own...

20:04.910 --> 20:06.280
Honey...

20:08.020 --> 20:11.440
I'm happy.

20:12.420 --> 20:15.250
It's finally time for the
two of us to drink together.

20:18.980 --> 20:20.790
Bye, Natsume.

20:20.790 --> 20:23.260
I'm glad I got to meet Reiko's grandson.

20:23.260 --> 20:24.450
Really...

20:27.250 --> 20:29.520
Don't make that face.

20:29.520 --> 20:32.430
Even if we can't make our cups,

20:32.430 --> 20:35.460
as long as we're together,
we'll continue our journey.

20:36.440 --> 20:39.730
Once you become a grown-up,
let's drink together!

20:42.350 --> 20:44.370
Thank you, Natsume!

20:44.370 --> 20:45.470
Thank you!

20:48.590 --> 20:50.050
I'm back.

20:52.390 --> 20:55.020
It's so late!

20:55.020 --> 20:56.940
You should've at least called...

20:58.300 --> 20:59.900
I'm sorry.

20:59.900 --> 21:02.000
What happened?

21:02.000 --> 21:03.700
You're covered in mud!

21:03.700 --> 21:05.500
No, um...

21:05.500 --> 21:07.710
Let's eat.

21:08.400 --> 21:10.700
Takashi, go wash your face.

21:10.700 --> 21:11.980
Okay.

21:11.980 --> 21:13.010
Shigeru-san.

21:13.010 --> 21:14.420
Now, now, Touko-san.

21:14.420 --> 21:16.670
We can hear the story while we eat.

21:16.670 --> 21:18.390
The food will get cold.

21:18.390 --> 21:19.650
But...

21:21.190 --> 21:22.550
You're right...
